===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:servise|tree=1}}

From {{inh|en|enm|servise}}, from {{inh|en|ang|serfis}}, from {{der|en|fro|servise}} ({{cog|fr|service}}), from the verb {{m|fro|servir}}, from {{der|en|la|servitium}} (compare {{cog|pt|serviço}}, {{cog|it|servizio}}, {{cog|nrf|sèrvice}}, {{cog|es|servicio}}), from {{m|la|servus||servant; serf; slave}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro||*ser-wo-s|guardian}}, possibly from {{m|ine-pro|*ser-||watch over, protect}}.<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=''n.''{{sup|1}}|noformat=1|id=1059809588}}</ref> Displaced native {{cog|ang|þeġnung}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# An [[act#Noun|act]] of being of [[assistance]] to someone.
#: {{ux|en|I say I did him a '''service''' by ending our relationship&nbsp;– now he can freely pursue his career.}}
#* {{RQ:Southey Wat Tyler|page=7|passage=The Parliament for ever cries ''more money'', / ''The '''service''' of the state demands more money.'' / Just heaven! of what '''service''' is the state?}}
#* {{RQ:Lincoln Pratt's Patients|chapter=4|passage=Then he commenced to talk, really talk. and inside of two flaps of a herring's fin he had me mesmerized, like Eben Holt's boy at the town hall show. He talked about the ills of humanity, and the glories of health and Nature and '''service''' and land knows what all.}}
# The state of being [[subordinate]] to or employed by an individual or group.
#: {{ux|en|Lancelot was at the '''service''' of King Arthur.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XX|33|The lesser griefs that may be said, / ⁠That breathe a thousand tender vows, / ⁠Are but as servants in a house / Where lies the master newly dead; / Who speak their feeling as it is, / ⁠And weep the fulness from the mind: / ⁠‘It will be hard’ they say ‘to find / Another '''service''' such as this.’}}
# {{senseid|en|military service, uncountable sense}} {{lb|en|[[Appendix:Glossary#ellipsis|elliptical]]|uncountable}} Work as a member of the [[military]].
#: {{syn|en|military service}}
#: {{ux|en|Thank you for your '''service'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Students were exempt from '''service''' in the [[armed forces]].}}
# {{senseid|en|a specific military, countable, with definite article}} {{lb|en|with|{{m|en|the}}}} The [[military]].
#: {{syn|en|forces|q1=plural noun}}
#: {{co|en|the '''service'''}}
#: {{ux|en|I did three years in the '''service''' before coming here.}}
# {{senseid|en|economic}} {{lb|en|economics}} The [[practice]] of providing assistance as economic activity.
#: {{ux|en|Hair care is a '''service''' industry.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-21|author=w:Oliver Burkeman
|volume=189|issue=2|page=27|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=The tao of tech
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/technology/2013/may/10/conscious-computing-twitter-facebook-google
|passage=The dirty secret of the internet is that all this distraction and interruption is immensely profitable. Web companies like to boast about [&hellip;], or offering '''services''' that let you "stay up to date with what your friends are doing",[...]and so on. But the real way to build a successful online business is to be better than your rivals at undermining people's control of their own attention.}}
# {{lb|en|business}} {{syn of|en|utility||[[commodity]] provided on a continuous basis by a physical infrastructure network, such as [[electricity]], [[water]] [[supply]] or [[sewerage]]}}.
# A department in a company, organization, or institution.
# {{lb|en|computing}} A [[function]] that is provided by one [[program]] or [[machine]] for another.
#: {{ux|en|This machine provides the name '''service''' for the LAN.}}
# {{anchor|silverware}}A [[set]] of [[dishes]] or [[utensils]].
#: {{ux|en|She brought out the silver tea '''service'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=w:Eduardo Galeano|title=[[w:Open Veins of Latin America|Open Veins of Latin America: Five Centuries of the Pillage of a Continent]]|publisher=Monthly Review Press|page=36
|passage=When their lavish fiestas ended they threw the '''silver service''' and even golden vessels from their balconies to be picked up by lucky passersby.}}
# {{lb|en|sports}} The act of initially starting, or serving, the [[ball]] in play in [[tennis]], [[volleyball]], and other games.
#: {{ux|en|The player had four '''service''' faults in the set.}}
# A religious [[rite]] or [[ritual]].
#* {{RQ:Maxwell Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=5|passage=Here, in the transept and choir, where the '''service''' was being held, one was conscious every moment of an increasing brightness; colours glowing vividly beneath the circular chandeliers, and the rows of small lights on the choristers' desks flashed and sparkled in front of the boys' faces, deep linen collars, and red neckbands.}}
#: {{ux|en|The funerary '''service''' was touching.}}
# {{lb|en|legal}} The serving, or delivery, of a [[summons]] or [[writ]].
#* '''1668''' July 3, [[w:James Dalrymple, 1st Viscount of Stair|James Dalrymple]], “Thomas Rue ''contra'' Andrew Houſtoun” in ''The Deciſions of the Lords of Council & Seſſion'' I (Edinburgh, 1683), [http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=7ApBAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA548&dq=%22correus%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=BFYCT56sNs7Z8QOstrGlAQ&ved=0CHAQ6AEwCQ#v=onepage&q=%22correus%22&f=false page 548]:
#*: He Suſpends on theſe Reaſons, that ''Thomas Rue'' had granted a general Diſcharge to ''Adam Muſhet'', who was his Conjunct, and ''correus debendi'', after the alleadged '''Service''', which Diſcharged ''Muſhet'', and conſequently ''Houstoun'' his Partner.
#: {{ux|en|The '''service''' happened yesterday.}}
# {{lb|en|Israel|West Bank|also in Jordan, Lebanon and Syria}}<!--don't turn the last three country names into labels, or they categorize--> A [[taxi]] [[share]]d among unrelated passengers, each of whom pays [[part]] of the [[fare]]; often, it has a fixed route between cities.
# A [[musical]] [[composition]] for use in [[church]]es.
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Profession of respect; acknowledgment of duty owed.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 8|III|i|passage=Pray, do my '''service''' to his majesty.}}
# {{lb|en|nautical}} The materials used for [[serve|serving]] a rope, etc., such as spun yarn and small lines.
# Access to resources such as hotel rooms and Web-based videos without transfer of the resources' ownership.

=====Usage notes=====
* In British English, the indefinite article ''a'' is often used with “good service”, as in "''A'' good service is operating on all London Underground lines", whereas this is not used in American English.

